---
const steps = [
  {
    lead: 'Pick a tool.',
    rest: 'Open the one you need. There is no signup, no trial, and no card on file.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Do the job in the tab.',
    rest: 'The work happens on your own machine, so a large file is not waiting on an upload.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Close it and move on.',
    rest: 'Nothing is stored, so there is nothing to delete afterwards.',
  },
];
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-content) px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">How it works</h2>

  <ol class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-6">
    {steps.map((step, i) => (
      <li class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <p class="font-body text-base text-fg-secondary">
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-fg">{step.lead}</span> {step.rest}
        </p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-10 max-w-[60ch] font-body text-sm text-muted">
    Your files are read by your browser and never sent to a server. That is not a policy promise, it is how the
    tools are built.
  </p>
</section>
